{"name":"Pestilence","hex":"#9f8303","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pestilence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The personification of pestilence, often depicted riding a white horse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pestilence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infection","blocks":[{"text":"An infection is the invasion of tissues by pathogens, their multiplication, and the reaction of host tissues to the infectious agent and the toxins they produce. An infectious disease is an illness resulting from an infection, and some infectious diseases are also communicable (transmissible)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Cutaneous_abscess_MRSA_staphylococcus_aureus_7826_lores.jpg/330px-Cutaneous_abscess_MRSA_staphylococcus_aureus_7826_lores.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infection","wikidata":"Q166231"},{"title":"Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse","blocks":[{"text":"The Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse are figures in the Book of Revelation in the New Testament of the Bible, a piece of apocalypse literature attributed to John of Patmos, and generally regarded as dating from about AD 95. Similar allusions are contained in the Old Testament books of Ezekiel and Zechariah, written centuries prior. Though the text only provides a name for the fourth horseman, subsequent commentary often identifies them as personifications of Conquest, War, Famine, and Death."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Apocalypse_vasnetsov.jpg/330px-Apocalypse_vasnetsov.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Horsemen_of_the_Apocalypse","wikidata":"Q58155"},{"title":"Pestilence (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Pestilence is a Dutch death metal band founded in Enschede in 1986. Despite various lineup changes, guitarist-vocalist Patrick Mameli remains the sole constant member. After disbanding in 1994 to pursue other musical directions, Pestilence reunited in 2008, but was put on \"permanent hold\" in July 2014. The band reunited again in October 2016. Pestilence has released ten studio albums, and are one of technical death metal's \"big four\", with Death, Atheist, and Cynic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Hellfest2019Pestilence_01.jpg/330px-Hellfest2019Pestilence_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pestilence_(band)","wikidata":"Q1066740"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Chain_of_Infection.png/500px-Chain_of_Infection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Chain_of_Infection.png/1280px-Chain_of_Infection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Chain_of_Infection.png/500px-Chain_of_Infection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chain of infection; the chain of events that lead to infection","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChain_of_Infection.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Dit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg/330px-Dit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Dit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg/330px-Dit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Infection of an ingrown toenail; there is pus (yellow) and resultant inflammation (redness and swelling around the nail).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki